## 5. Edge Case Catalog

| # | Scenario | Detection | Behavior |
|---|----------|-----------|----------|
| EC-01 | Not a git repo | `discover.js` checks `.git/` | Skip hooks + husky-init. Warn. Continue with sync only. |
| EC-02 | Consumer has NO package.json | `discover.js` read attempt fails | Warn. Skip prepare phase. Continue with hooks + sync. |
| EC-03 | Consumer's pre-commit is a Python script | `hooks.js` checks first line for `#!/` + non-sh shebang | Create wrapper shell script. Don't modify original. |
| EC-04 | Consumer's pre-commit is a compiled binary | `hooks.js` stat check + file magic | Create wrapper. Warn. |
| EC-05 | Consumer has `"prepare": "my-script && husky"` | `prepare.js` detects "husky" substring | Skip. Already configured. |
| EC-06 | Consumer has multi-line prepare script | `prepare.js` detects newline in string | Warn. Provide manual instructions. |
| EC-07 | npm v12 blocks postinstall | User explicitly runs `npx setup` | No change needed — setup is explicit. |
| EC-08 | Running in GitHub Actions | `discover.js` checks `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` | Skip hooks. Only sync + scaffold memory-bank. |
| EC-09 | Consumer has husky v8 (not v9) | `husky-init.js` checks husky version | Warn: "Husky v9+ required. You have v8. Upgrade: npm install husky@9" |
| EC-10 | Consumer's .husky/ is a file, not directory | `hooks.js` stat check | Error: ".husky/ exists as a file, not a directory. Remove it first." |
| EC-11 | Permission denied writing .husky/ | `hooks.js` write fails | Error: "Permission denied. Check file ownership." |
| EC-12 | git config fails (permission) | `husky-init.js` exec fails | Warn. Provide manual command. |
| EC-13 | package.json is malformed JSON | `discover.js` / `prepare.js` parse fails | Error: "package.json is not valid JSON." |
| EC-14 | Consumer project is the template itself | `discover.js` checks if consumerRoot === packageRoot | Warn: "Running setup on the template itself. Some steps will be skipped." |
| EC-15 | Dry-run in CI | Multiple flags combine | Report what WOULD happen (hooks skipped, sync would run). |
| EC-16 | Consumer has `node_modules/.bin/husky` but husky is not in dependencies | `husky-init.js` resolves husky | It still works — husky is available. No warn needed. |
| EC-17 | Consumer has `.husky/_/` from a previous husky version | `husky-init.js` — husky() handles this | Husky re-generates shims. Existing `_/` is overwritten. |
| EC-18 | Consumer hook file is empty | `hooks.js` size === 0 | Treat as "not our hook" → append. |
| EC-19 | Consumer has `"prepare": "husky || true"` | `prepare.js` detects "husky" substring | Skip (already contains husky). Considered "configured." |
| EC-20 | INIT_CWD is undefined (not run via npx) | `discover.js` fallback to cwd() | Warn: "Running outside npx context. Using current directory." |

---

## 6. UX Copy

### 6.1 Banner

```
@abarcenas/ai-workflow-template v1.29.0 — setup

This command installs AI workflow tooling into your project:
  • Git hooks (pre-commit, post-merge) via husky
  • .agents/ and .opencode/ configuration files
  • Memory bank scaffolding
  • Prepare script configuration

Documentation: https://github.com/abarcenas29/ai-workflow-template#readme
```

### 6.2 Help Text

```
Usage: npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup [options]

Options:
  --force         Overwrite existing hooks and prepare script
  --dry-run       Report what would happen without making changes
  --yes, -y       Skip all confirmation prompts (non-interactive mode)
  --skip-hooks    Skip git hook installation
  --skip-prepare  Skip prepare script modification
  --skip-sync     Skip file sync and memory bank scaffold
  --quiet, -q     Only show errors
  --verbose, -V   Show all output including debug information
  --help, -h      Show this help message
  --version, -v   Show version number

Examples:
  npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup           # Standard setup
  npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup --force    # Overwrite existing config
  npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup --dry-run  # Preview changes
  npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup --yes      # Non-interactive (CI/CD)
```

### 6.3 Warning Messages

```
⚠  Not a git repository — git hooks will NOT be installed.
   Run `git init` first, then re-run setup.

⚠  Your prepare script is complex and could not be automatically merged.
   Add '&& husky' to your prepare script manually:
   "scripts": { "prepare": "<your-script> && husky" }

⚠  Husky v9+ is required. Your version may be incompatible.
   Upgrade: npm install husky@9 --save-dev

⚠  Running setup on the template project itself.
   Some steps will be skipped as they are not applicable.

⚠  Running outside npx context. Using the current directory as the target.
   For best results, run via: npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup

⚠  Already normalized. Use --force to re-run normalization.
```

### 6.4 Error Messages

```
✗  .husky/ exists as a file, not a directory.
   Remove it first: rm .husky

✗  package.json is not valid JSON.
   Fix the syntax error and re-run setup.

✗  Permission denied writing to .husky/pre-commit.
   Check file ownership and permissions.

✗  Husky is not installed in this project.
   Run: npm install husky --save-dev
   Then re-run: npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup
```

### 6.5 Success Messages

```
✓  pre-commit hook installed

✓  pre-commit hook merged (your existing hook is preserved)

✓  prepare script already set to "husky"

✓  Husky initialized — git hooks are active

✓  12 files synced (3 new), 6 memory-bank files scaffolded
```

### 6.6 Promotion (shown at end, only once per session)

```
💡 Enjoying ai-workflow-template? Star us on GitHub:
   https://github.com/abarcenas29/ai-workflow-template

   Run `npx @abarcenas/ai-workflow-template setup` anytime to update.
```

